I've been thinking some more about Polish terminology. Koszula means shirt. Koszula necessarily is a button-down thing and has long sleeves. Koszulka (literally, little shirt) by definition has short sleeves or no sleeves at all. We usually add a descriptor to koszulka to make it clear which kind we mean (like koszulka z krótkim rękawem forma t-shirt), but if I heard somebody about simply "koszulka", I'd assume it was a tee. Koszulka and koszula may be either a male, female or unise× thing. Bluzka (blouse) is female only. Now, I don't really grasp what makes a garment a bluzka rather than a koszulka...

